cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AmpliTrim, please cite it as below."
title: "AmpliTrim: choosing DADA2 truncation lengths and maxEE from the reads themselves"
type: software
version: "0.4.1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23860406"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/paytonyau/amplitrim"
abstract: >-
  AmpliTrim recommends DADA2 truncLenF, truncLenR and maxEE for paired-end amplicon reads and tests candidate settings on the user's own reads: it replicates DADA2's
  quality filter from the quality scores, sets a coverage floor from the amplicon lengths, estimates the merge yield with vsearch, and chooses maxEE per read from the reads' expected errors. For ITS it advises trimming the poor read ends with a sliding window before DADA2, keeps maxEE at 2 for the trimmed reads, and otherwise computes maxEE the same way.
authors:
  - family-names: "Yau"
    given-names: "Payton (Tung On)"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3283-0370"
keywords:
  - DADA2
  - amplicon sequencing
  - 16S rRNA
  - ITS
  - paired-end reads
